Description: Fortran library for mathematics, science and engineering (development files)
 SciFortran is a collection of Fortran modules and procedures for scientific
 calculations, loosely modelled on SciPy: linear algebra (dense and sparse),
 FFT, integration, interpolation, minimisation and root finding, special
 functions, random numbers, I/O and plotting helpers, and MPI/ScaLAPACK
 wrappers.
 .
 This package provides the static library (libscifor.a), the Fortran module
 files and a pkg-config file. Build against it with, for example:
 .
   mpif90 $(pkg-config --cflags scifor) prog.f90 $(pkg-config --libs scifor)
 .
 The Fortran module files are specific to the gfortran module format they
 were built with, and the library is built for the default MPI implementation.
 BLAS and LAPACK are used through the system alternatives, so any
 implementation (reference, OpenBLAS, ...) can be selected at run time.
 The non-free Intel MKL is neither required nor used.
